  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.30.19 - AM030 DI-injected converter false-positive suppression\n\n            Changed:\n            - Hardened AM030 unused-converter detection so a declared `ITypeConverter<TSource, TDestination>` is no longer reported as unused when any `ConvertUsing(...)` argument resolves to the interface `ITypeConverter<TSource, TDestination>` itself (covers constructor injection, service-locator resolution, and other DI shapes whose concrete implementation cannot be statically traced)\n            - The existing concrete-converter detection (via `ConvertUsing<TConverter>()`, `typeof(...)`, `new ...()`, or interface-typed locals/fields/properties with concrete initializers) remains untouched, so declared converters that no `ConvertUsing` call references — including ones with a different `<TSource, TDestination>` pair — still report\n\n            Validation:\n            - Full solution test suite passing on net10.0 with targeted AM030 and RuleCatalog coverage\n            - Rule catalog and sample diagnostics snapshot checks passing\n            - git diff --check clean\n\n            Previous Release: v2.30.18 - AM031 LINQ enumeration coverage",
